---
// The proved theorems (/science/prove2me/theorems/): every leaf of prove2me that prove2me accepted a proof of, newest
// first, with the denominator, the selection from trial 11 on and three costs, all computed from the same records as
// the prove2me page (prove2me-theorems.ts). The build fetches the records (prove2me-build.ts; its committed copy when
// the gateway does not answer), and the browser reads them again every minute (scripts/theorems-live.ts). Statements in
// plain English are not written yet: each row links to the theorem's statement on prove2me.
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { p2m } from '../../../../data/prove2me';
import { THEOREMS_PATH, costsHTML, selectionText, theoremKpisHTML, theoremRowsHTML, updatedText } from '../../../../data/prove2me-theorems';
import { buildTheorems } from '../../../../data/prove2me-theorems-build';
import '../../../../styles/theorems.css';

const { history, view, from, pages } = await buildTheorems();
const leaves = pages.map((t) => t.leaf);
const kp = theoremKpisHTML(view);
const known = { history, pages: leaves };
const image = new URL(`${THEOREMS_PATH}og.png`, Astro.site).href;
const imageAlt = `${view.counts.proofs} Lean proofs by ${p2m.model} accepted by prove2me, and what each cost in GPU-hours.`;
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Proved theorems',
		head: [
			{ tag: 'title', content: `Lean theorems ${p2m.model} proved on prove2me - AIs@home` },
			{ tag: 'meta', attrs: { property: 'og:image', content: image } },
			{ tag: 'meta', attrs: { property: 'og:image:alt', content: imageAlt } },
			{ tag: 'meta', attrs: { name: 'twitter:image:alt', content: imageAlt } },
		],
		description: `Every leaf of prove2me, research theorems stated in Lean 4, that ${p2m.model}, an open model on the AIs@home network, proved and prove2me accepted: how many were tried, and what a proof costs in GPU-hours.`,
	}}
	headings={[
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'counts', text: 'What the count means' },
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'cost', text: 'What a proof costs' },
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'theorems', text: 'Every accepted leaf' },
		{ depth: 2, slug: 'data', text: 'The data' },
	]}
>
	<p>
		<a href="https://prove2.me/">prove2me</a> collects theorems from mathematical research papers, stated in Lean 4 by its users and split into
		small pieces called leaves. A leaf is one step toward a paper’s result, not the result itself. {p2m.model}, an open-weight model
		on the AIs@home network, works on open leaves as an agent; Lean’s kernel checks each proof, and prove2me’s own check decides
		whether to accept it. These are the leaves it accepted. More on how the trials run is on the <a href="/science/prove2me/">prove2me page</a>.
	</p>
	<p class="th-updated" data-th-updated data-source="build">{updatedText(view, from === 'snapshot' ? 'saved' : 'build')}</p>
	<script is:inline type="application/json" data-th-known set:html={JSON.stringify(known).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')} />

	<dl class="th-kpis not-content" data-th-kpis data-source="build" style={`--kpis: ${kp.n}`} set:html={kp.html} />

	<h2 id="counts">What the count means</h2>
	<p data-th-selection>{selectionText(view)}</p>
	<p>
		A leaf closed by reuse is one whose accepted proof is a theorem someone else had already proved on prove2me: we submitted the
		proof that uses it and name its author. It is listed below, marked, and counted neither as a proof by the model nor in the costs.
	</p>

	<h2 id="cost">What a proof costs</h2>
	<dl class="th-costs not-content" data-th-costs data-source="build" style="--kpis: 3" set:html={costsHTML(view)} />
	<p class="th-note">
		A GPU-hour here is an hour of the model generating on one GPU, summed over a run’s tasks; Lean’s checks and the agent’s own time
		are not counted, and tasks stopped before they finished are missing from the records, so all three are slight undercounts.
		Benches, which run leaves of earlier trials again on a newer scaffold, are not counted. Part of the fall in cost since
		trial {view.counts.selected.from} comes from choosing easier leaves (above), not only from a better scaffold. All three numbers are computed from the records each time the page
		reads them.
	</p>

	<h2 id="theorems">Every accepted leaf</h2>
	<p>
		<span data-th-count>{view.theorems.length}</span> leaves, newest first. Each statement is on prove2me for now; plain-English statements
		are not written yet. A leaf accepted since the site’s last build appears here at once, and gets its own page at the next build.
	</p>
	<div class="th-wrap not-content">
		<table class="th-table">
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Leaf</th><th scope="col">Theorem and statement</th><th scope="col">Accepted</th><th scope="col" class="num" title="GPU-hours of the leaf’s own tasks">GPU-h</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody data-th-rows data-source="build" set:html={theoremRowsHTML(view, new Set(leaves))} />
		</table>
	</div>
	<p class="th-note">
		GPU-hours and tokens of a leaf are those of its own tasks in the trial that proved it; earlier failed tries of the same leaf count in
		the all-in costs above, not here.
	</p>

	<h2 id="data">The data</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>This page as JSON: <a href="/science/prove2me/theorems.json"><code>/science/prove2me/theorems.json</code></a> (as of the site’s build), and each leaf’s at <code>/science/prove2me/theorems/&lt;leaf&gt;.json</code>.</li>
		<li>
			The gateway’s public records, which this page reads every minute:
			{' '}<a href="/v1/projects/prove2me/results"><code>results</code></a> (prove2me’s verdicts; a reuse carries a <code>reuse</code> record),
			{' '}<a href="/v1/projects/prove2me/campaigns"><code>campaigns</code></a> (the trials and their leaves) and
			{' '}<a href="/v1/tasks?project=prove2me"><code>tasks</code></a> (each task’s model minutes and tokens).
		</li>
		<li>Every leaf tried, failed runs included, and every task: the <a href="/science/prove2me/#leaves">prove2me page</a>.</li>
	</ul>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
	import { liveTheorems } from '../../../../scripts/theorems-live';
	liveTheorems();
</script>
